Subject: [PATCH 26/27] docs: T2's happy path verified live, against a
 reference read outside Tallow
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The binding was already verified for refusals offline; its happy path was recorded as
unverified because it fetches and no local fixture can be. It is verified now, and the
method is the record's point: the reference was read independently through Tor before the
run, so the result is evidence rather than two engines agreeing with each other.

Both legs exited 0 (the native one under --require-native, so no fallback), produced
byte-identical output, and the seed_url matched the independently-read first <loc> of a
real 84-entry sitemap. The compiled path did that fetch itself, over the Tor plane proven
beforehand.

Two details kept because they cost time to learn: the CLI binary had to be rebuilt first,
since cargo check and cargo test do not produce one and the pre-existing binary predated
the arm — testing against it would have reported a bogus "native build unavailable"; and
the live fixture stays out of the repo, because a suite that needs Tor up is a suite that
fails for reasons unrelated to the code.
